SUMMARY:Seminar: "A Field Guide to Watersheds: Division and Unity" by Eli
 za Griswold
DESCRIPTION:Eliza Griswold is a Pulitzer Prize-winning journalist and dir
 ector of the Program in Journalism at Princeton. As a basic building blo
 ck of systems theory\, the concept of a watershed defines and divides\; 
 it also unifies. While researching her book Amity & Prosperity\, One Fam
 ily and the Fracturing of America\, which was awarded the Pulitzer Prize
 \, Griswold spent seven years reporting inside a watershed made up of co
 ncerned citizen-scientists\, farmers\, and families contending with the 
 unintended consequences of unconventional oil and gas development. Grisw
 old explored the realities and metaphors o\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/ev
 ents/2026/seminar-field-guide-watersheds-division-and-unity-eliza-griswo
 ld
