SUMMARY:Staying Alive in Hitler’s Berlin
DESCRIPTION:Hitler never trusted Berliners\, and many Berliners never tru
 sted him. Berlin was the cosmopolitan metropolis which the Nazis liked t
 o hate. Too many free spirits\, too many sexual deviants\, and too many 
 Jews. When the Third Reich was finally defeated in May 1945\, the city w
 as in ruins. Bleiben Sie übrig\, ‘stay alive’\, is how Berliners sa
 id goodbye to each once British and American bombers attacked the city d
 ay and night. By that stage\, in 1943\, most Jews of Berlin had already 
 been deported to the death camps. If my book about daily life in Hitler
 ’s capital during the war has a running theme\, it\nhttps://www.prince
 ton.edu/events/2026/staying-alive-hitlers-berlin
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/staying-alive-hitlers-berlin
