 l impacts raise urgent questions about its future. After Concrete: Rethi
 nking the Dynamics of a Material (Birkhäuser\, 2026) brings together es
 says by interdisciplinary scholars to examine concrete’s next chapter\
 , investigating how its sustainability will draw both from innovative re
 search and past solutions. On October 29\, 2026\, at the Princeton Unive
 rsity School of Architecture\, the book’s three co-editors—Lucia All
 ais\, Michael Faciejew\, and Forrest Meggers—will \nhttps://www.prince
