  Lessons from Nicaragua's Sugarcane Zone
DESCRIPTION:his talk will focus on fieldwork from Nicaragua to discuss me
 dical anthropology's contribution to the emerging interdisciplinary fiel
 d of planetary health. One of the consequences of climate change is a ne
 w form of disease emergence\, in which ostensibly noncommunicable diseas
 es become epidemics as ecological damage accretes in specific landscapes
 . Linking Alex's work on an epidemic of chronic kidney disease to previo
 us research on (communicable) mosquito-borne disease in Nicaragua\, he s
 uggests that attention to the landscape\, its structures\, and its tempo
