SUMMARY:Fund for Irish Studies: Conversation with Yiyun Li — Music Agai
 nst the Night
DESCRIPTION:Yiyun Li\, Pulitzer Prize winner and Princeton Professor of C
 reative Writing\, launches her new novel\, Music Against the Night\, a h
 istorical saga tracing the life of Irish composer and pianist John Field
  (1782–1837). Known as the inventor of the nocturne\, Field is portray
 ed from his musical upbringing in Dublin to his success in Russia. The s
 tory follows his artistic development\, personal struggles\, and legacy.
  Li will read briefly from the novel and be in conversation with Princet
 on Professor of Music Donnacha M. Dennehy\, and pianist Cristina Altamur
 a will play a John Field nocturne and an earl\nhttps://www.princeton.edu
 /events/2026/fund-irish-studies-conversation-yiyun-li-music-against-nigh
