SUMMARY:Ahilan Kadirgamar | Crises\, Struggles and Alternatives: The Long
  Twentieth Century of Youth Movements in Sri Lanka
DESCRIPTION:Beginning with the Jaffna Youth Congress and its anti-colonia
 l politics in the 1920s\, Sri Lanka has been transformed by youth strugg
 les\, including the recent uprising in 2022\; where youth from all commu
 nities – the Muslim and Hill Country Tamil minorities joined en masse 
 with the Sinhala majority – chased away an authoritarian president. Ma
 ny youth movements emerged during crisis times\, and some were defeated 
 by brutal counter revolutions. The LSSP\, the first left party in the co
 untry\, was forged with youth activism during the Great Depression and t
 he malaria epidemic in the mid-1930s. The ant\nhttps://www.princeton.edu
 /events/2026/ahilan-kadirgamar-crises-struggles-and-alternatives-long-tw
 entieth-century-youth
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/ahilan-kadirgamar-crises-strugg
 les-and-alternatives-long-twentieth-century-youth
