SUMMARY:Designing Presentations That Work
DESCRIPTION:Ever look at a slide and know something isn’t working\, but
  you’re not sure why? This workshop will cover practical ways to make 
 presentations clearer\, cleaner\, and easier to follow. We’ll look at 
 layout\, fonts\, color\, images\, accessibility\, and common design mist
 akes\, using before-and-after examples to show how simple changes can ma
 ke a big difference. Presented by Lisa Jackson\, Senior Producer / Produ
 ction Manager\, Digital Learning and Design at the McGraw Center for Tea
 ching and Learning\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/designing-pres
 entations-work
