SUMMARY:Japanese Woodblock Printing
DESCRIPTION:This workshop will provide an overview of the materials\, too
 ls\, and practices of historical Japanese woodblock printing. Participan
 ts will also learn about modern-day technologies (e.g.\, 3D printing and
  laser cutting) used to replicate select historical woodblock prints hel
 d by the Marquand Library and featured in the current Milberg Gallery ex
 hibition\, “The Art of Japanese Publishing.” After a brief introduct
 ion to the exhibition and a demonstration of the technique\, multiple bl
 ocks will be available for participants to make their own woodblock prin
 ts. Instructors: Ariel Ackerly and Molly Dot\nhttps://www.princeton.edu/
 events/2026/japanese-woodblock-printing
URL:https://www.princeton.edu/events/2026/japanese-woodblock-printing
