SUMMARY:Pop-Up Talk: Curator Kit Brooks
DESCRIPTION:Short talks and Q&As on Museum topics This month\, Kit Brooks
 \, the Museum's curator of Asian art\, will discuss the special exhibiti
 on "Takeda Hideo’s Genpei: Defying Authority\," which features a serie
 s of silkscreen prints that cynically reinterprets Japan’s Genpei War 
 (1180–85) within the context of twentieth-century social upheavals. Af
 ter the talk\, head upstairs to the Allen Adler and Frances Beatty Adler
  Gallery for an informal conversation with the curator.\nhttps://www.pri
 nceton.edu/events/2026/pop-talk-curator-kit-brooks
