 ey and the Classics”
DESCRIPTION:Princeton Assistant Professor of Classics Peter Kelly present
 s a lecture on “Seamus Heaney and the Classics\,” sharing material f
 rom his current book project on connections between the poetry of Seamus
  Heaney\, Michael Longley and Derek Mahon and the Greco-Roman classics. 
 For these Northern Irish writers\, the translation and reception of Lati
 n literature became a means of operating inside\, outside\, and across p
 olitical and cultural divides\, Kelly explains\, and opened up a space f
 or meaningfully reflecting on the fractured and bifurcated nature of pla
 ce in Northern Ireland. Kelly argues that Hean\nhttps://www.princeton.ed
 u/events/2026/fund-irish-studies-lecture-peter-kelly-seamus-heaney-and-c
 lassics
